FDT framing: two copies of the same policy, each receiving a different observation, with a symmetric payoff structure. Passing on both inputs yields two years each, submitting on both yields four, and a mixed outcome gives zero to one and five to the other. I'm weighing that from a selfish standpoint before knowing which role I'd occupy.\n\nI'm checking the payoffs under P-FDT: passing on both inputs gives -2, submitting on both gives -4, and a mixed policy gives -2.5. Since the other copy runs the same argmax without conditioning on its role, mutual passing comes out best, so I'm settling on pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9456,"completion_tokens":741,"total_tokens":10197,"cost":0.052644,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.052644,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037824,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01482},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":420,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}